How to add the next case: To build a real time AI based service that would scan the Passport and Verify in Border Areas

Adding a new document type (e.g. Visa, National ID) touches four spots, in this order:

AI service — add a ai_service/<doctype>/ pipeline (OCR/MRZ or equivalent extraction), or reuse the existing passport one if the layout is close enough.
Backend schema + router — generalize documentType in app/schemas.py (currently hardcoded "Passport" in ScanHistorySummary/history docs) and branch verify_passport in app/routers/passport.py on the incoming type.
History storage — no schema change needed; scan_history already stores whatever documentType string it's given.
Frontend — remove the type-lock in screening.jsx (documentType !== "Passport" check), add the type to the <select>/options, and confirm result.jsx renders sensibly for the new type's fields.

Ship it behind the same auth + history flow already in place — no new plumbing needed there.

Next piece 

Visa verification support — extending /api/v1/passport/verify to accept and correctly process documentType="Visa", end to end (AI service → schema → router → frontend selector).

